<p class="lead">Most studios start on a booking platform, and that's sensible. As the studio grows, owners notice the downsides: their brand sits inside someone else's app, clients see other studios nearby, and pricing has to fit the platform's options. Here is when a fitness studio booking app of your own makes sense.</p>
<h2 id="what-a-branded-app-gives-you">What a branded app gives you</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Your brand, on the client's home screen, with no other studios listed beside you.</li>
  <li>Your customer data and relationship, including messages and offers on your terms.</li>
  <li>Your pricing: intro offers, class packs, memberships and bundles exactly as you run them.</li>
  <li>Something different: for example, guidance between sessions. One pilates platform we built includes an AI instructor that guides clients through their sessions.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="what-it-costs-to-run">What it costs to run</h2>
<p>Beyond the build, plan for:</p>
<ul>
  <li>hosting and monitoring</li>
  <li>Apple and Google developer accounts</li>
  <li>payment processing fees</li>
  <li>updates when phone operating systems change</li>
  <li>someone to answer support questions</li>
</ul>
<p>Compare that with your current platform fees as you grow, not just today.</p>
<h2 id="features-that-matter-most">Features that matter most</h2>
<ol>
  <li>A fast weekly schedule with one-tap booking.</li>
  <li>Class packs, memberships and intro offers.</li>
  <li>Waitlists that fill spots automatically.</li>
  <li>Late-cancel and no-show rules applied fairly.</li>
  <li>Reminders and "spot opened" notifications.</li>
  <li>An admin view for instructors, classes and payments.</li>
</ol>
<p>The rules behind items 2 to 4 cause the most trouble, so we wrote a separate guide on <a href="/blogs/class-booking-memberships-waitlists">class packs, memberships and waitlists</a>.</p>
<h2 id="when-to-stay-on-a-platform">When to stay on a platform</h2>
<p>If you run one location, standard pricing and no plans for features of your own, a platform is cheaper and simpler. Build when the platform is shaping your business instead of supporting it. See what we build on our <a href="/solutions/fitness-studios">fitness studios page</a>.</p>
<p>Thinking about your own studio app? <a href="/contact">Book a 30-min call</a> and we'll help you decide whether it's worth it at your size.</p>
